   "daf": "33a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "מִפְּנֵי שֶׁהֵן בּוֹעֲלֵי נִדּוֹת וְכוּ׳. אַטּוּ כּוּלְּהוּ בּוֹעֲלֵי נִדּוֹת נִינְהוּ? אָמַר רַבִּי יִצְחָק מַגְדְּלָאָה: בִּנְשׂוּאוֹת שָׁנוּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the impurity of Samaritan men is «due to» the fact «that» Samaritan men are considered men who «engage in intercourse with menstruating women,» and this is because they observe the seven-day menstrual period of impurity for each and every emission of blood. The Gemara asks: «Is this to say» that «all» Samaritan men «are» considered men who «engage in intercourse with menstruating women?» Aren’t there some unmarried men who do not engage in intercourse with menstruating women? «Rabbi Yitzḥak of Migdal says: They taught» this halakha only «with regard to» men to whom women are «married.»"
  }
